  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to combine resources from the proponent organization and the input from relevant collaborators. It will rehabilitate an existing space of Di&#xe1;logo Intercultural de M&#xe9;xico Activo AC (DIMA) to a place where refugee students will be able to sell products and organize other income generating events and activities. Aguascalientes is the base of DIMA, and current home to its 19 beneficiaries from various backgrounds, including Syria, Central America and Venezuela.</narrative>
  </description>
